# Weighted Visit-Scheduling Architecture: Logic, Formulae & Workflow

## 1. Overview

This document formalizes the visit-assignment logic discussed in the ESD lab workflow, combining hard constraints observed in real scheduling cases (for example, the 5034/5035 twins scenario) with a weighted scoring model inspired by the CSBS clinician-assignment rule.

The policy operates in three sequential layers:

1. Hard-constraint filtering
2. Weighted ranking
3. Tie-breaking and manual escalation

These layers ensure that no assignment is made unless the candidate is both eligible and appropriately ranked, while preserving human judgment for sensitive or high-risk cases.

---

## 2. Notation and Symbol Definitions

Let:

- $i \in \mathcal{C}$ denote a candidate
- $v \in \mathcal{V}$ denote a visit request
- $f$ denote the family associated with the visit
- $\Delta t_i$ denote the number of days since candidate $i$'s most recent assignment
- $n_{i,f}$ denote the number of prior visits candidate $i$ has completed with family $f$
- $\sigma_f \in \{-1, +1\}$ denote the family-specific continuity preference flag
- $d_{i,v}$ denote the estimated round-trip travel distance for candidate $i$ to visit $v$
- $v_i^{(\text{period})}$ denote candidate $i$'s visit count in the current review period
- $v_{\max}^{(\text{period})}$ denote the maximum visit count among active candidates in that period
- $\epsilon$ denote the score-tolerance threshold for tie detection

The assignment policy is defined over the eligible candidate set $\mathcal{E}_v$.

---

## 3. End-to-End Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[New Visit Request<br/>Family ID, Visit Type, Date Window] --> B[Layer 1: Hard Constraints]

    B --> B1[Availability Check<br/>candidate has open slot in the date window]
    B1 --> B2[Relationship Exclusion Check<br/>remove family-excluded candidates]
    B2 --> B3[Role/Certification Check<br/>candidate meets required visit type credential]
    B3 --> B4[Logistics Feasibility Check<br/>vehicle / transport requirement satisfied]

    B4 --> C{Any eligible candidates remain?}
    C -- No --> C1[Escalate to Coordinator<br/>manual rescheduling]
    C -- Yes --> D[Layer 2: Weighted Scoring]

    D --> D1[Compute $R_{i,v}$]
    D --> D2[Compute $F_{i,f}$]
    D --> D3[Compute $D_{i,v}$]
    D --> D4[Compute $L_i$]
    D --> D5[Compute $C_{i,f}$]

    D1 --> E[Composite score<br/>$S_{i,v} = \sum_k w_k x_k$]
    D2 --> E
    D3 --> E
    D4 --> E
    D5 --> E

    E --> F{Top two scores within $\epsilon$?}
    F -- Yes --> F1[Layer 3: Tie-break rule<br/>minimize or maximize family history depending on $\sigma_f$]
    F -- No --> G[Select top-scoring candidate]
    F1 --> G

    G --> H{Sensitive case? <br/>dual relationship, PI hold, or family preference}
    H -- Yes --> H1[Route to PI / Coordinator<br/>for manual confirmation]
    H -- No --> I[Auto-confirm assignment]

    H1 --> J[Log assignment]
    I --> J
    J --> K[Update recency, workload,<br/>and family-history records]
```

